# Strict-zero lane reports. Every writer defaults --out-json/--out-md to a
# cwd-relative path, so running a lane CLI (or `bash scripts/verify`, whose
# suite drives those CLIs) drops them into whatever directory you were in.
# CI publishes the real ones as workflow artifacts and the readers -- rollup
# `--artifacts-dir` and the coverage-gate baseline ZIP -- take them from there,
# never from a committed copy. Keeping them out of git also stops a local run
# from staging timestamp-only noise into an unrelated PR.
# NOTE: quality-rollup/ is ignored as a whole. If a curated (non-generated) file
# ever needs to live there -- e.g. quality-rollup/coverage-trend.json, which
# publish-admin-dashboard.yml and scheduled-alerts.yml read but nothing in this
# repo writes -- add an explicit "!quality-rollup/<file>" negation below.
coverage-100/
deepsource-visible-zero/
deps-zero/
qlty-zero/
quality-rollup/
quality-zero-gate/
run.json
